      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course, let's give these characters some depth and authenticity shaped by their environments:\n\n4. Ricky \"Ace\" Thompson – Ricky comes from a working-class neighborhood where numbers are king, and trust is harder to come by than oven-baked bread. Ethnic heritage gives Ricky a unique edge; he was born Afro-Caribbean but has found his adopted home in one of London's tightest thugs' circles. Especially known for his quick-fix hustles, Ace has less heart and more grit. He knows every alley and darkened corner of his borough, a trait that has earned him the nickname \"Ace.\" Ricky's expertise in skimming through risky business deals, and his calls from the corners by his streetlights, is both a curse and a survival skill in London's underbelly.\n\n5. Marco \"El Toro\" Rossi – This Italian connection came because both his granddad and great-granddad jumped to the UK. Born in the East End, Marco found his calling in the underground fight clubs, using aggression and sheer strength to survive. He grew up speaking little English but more about respect. His brutal talent makes him feel like an untamed bull in the china industry, but he always keeps his eye on rebuilding his family's reputation.\n\n6.",
